    "[THIS PRODUCT] Each 5.3 oz package contains approximately 5 servings of about 6 cookies each (around 30 cookies total).",
    "[GENERAL] Pizzelle originated in the Abruzzo region of central Italy and are traditionally baked by pressing batter between two hot, intricately patterned iron plates.",
    "[GENERAL] Unlike Dutch stroopwafels, which are dense, chewy, and layered with caramel syrup, Italian pizzelle are thin, dry, and crisp wafer-style cookies.",
    "[GENERAL] Because of their porous, wafer-like structure, pizzelle are classic companions for hot espresso, coffee, or tea, and can be dipped quickly or rested across the cup rim to soften slightly in the rising steam.",
    "[GENERAL] In addition to hot drinks, crisp chocolate pizzelle are traditionally served alongside after-dinner liqueurs or used as bookends for gelato sandwiches."
